<title>USA: TABLE - ML Bancorp Inc Q1 net, share rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - ML Bancorp Inc Q1 net, share rise.</headline>
<dateline>VILLANOVA, Pa. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands)</p>
<p>For the three months ended, June 30,</p>
<p>						1997		     1996</p>
<p> Interest Income			$36,790		 $33,526</p>
<p> Interest Expense			21,347		  20,456</p>
<p> Net Interest Income		   15,443		  13,070</p>
<p> Provision for Loan Losses	    1,050		   1,000</p>
<p>Net Interest Income after</p>
<p>  Provision for Loan Losses	  14,393		  12,070</p>
<p> Non-Interest Income		    4,328		   4,164</p>
<p> Non-Interest Expenses		 12,032		  11,559</p>
<p> Income before Income Taxes	   6,689		   4,675</p>
<p> Provision for Income Taxes	   2,935		   1,430</p>
<p> Net Income				 3,754		   3,245</p>
<p> Primary earnings per share(A)	 0.34		    0.27</p>
<p>Fully diluted earnings per share(A)</p>
<p>						 0.33		    0.27</p>
<p> Cash earnings per share(B)	    0.38		    0.37</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares Outstanding(A)</p>
<p>    -- Primary(A)			11,197		  12,039</p>
<p>    -- Fully diluted(A)		11,291		  12,049</p>
<p>Shares Outstanding, Period End(A)</p>
<p>					     10,566		  11,630</p>
<p>SELECTED FINANCIAL RATIOS</p>
<p> Net Interest Margin		    3.26%		   3.01%</p>
<p> Return on Average Assets	     0.75%		   0.71%</p>
<p> Return on Average Equity	    10.64%		   9.01%</p>
<p> Efficiency Ratio			61.54%		  68.30%</p>
<p>NOTES: (A) All shares and per share data adjusted for two-for-one stock split in September 1996.</p>
<p>(B) EPS adjusted for goodwill amortization and stock benefit plans expense.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610.</p>
